id: pm-v0a0un
title: Assurance mutation refusals cross the CLI as unclassified Sentry faults (PM-CLI-2Y/2Z/30)
description: "Three fresh handled assurance CRUD failures are emitted as high unclassified_runtime_error events: malformed definitions can dereference missing fields with raw TypeError, removing a gate-owned assertion throws raw TypeError, and weakening an assertion without an authorized terminal Decision throws raw TypeError. These are deterministic user-facing mutation refusals, so they must cross CLI/SDK/MCP hosts as typed usage errors while evaluator and storage faults remain fail-closed."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: "area:assurance","area:observability",error-taxonomy,release-gate,sentry
created_at: "2026-08-11T15:52:37.247Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-11T16:25:27.201Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-11T16:21:50.348Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-11T16:21:50.348Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: Assurance put/remove definition and reference refusals return PmCliError with usage exit semantics across the shared action transport; malformed nested definitions never crash on trim; genuine evaluator/storage faults remain unexpected; regression tests cover the three live fault classes; the live reliability limitation is recorded without resolving external Sentry state prematurely
outcome: "Assurance user refusals are typed, machine-classifiable, host-consistent, and absent from unexpected-error capture."
why_now: The final live Sentry gate found three fresh unresolved high issues after the broad SDK tranche passed all local gates.
parent: pm-1jzupz
risk: high
confidence: high
severity: high
environment: published 2026.8.11 assurance CLI dogfood
repro_steps: "Run assurance put with a malformed assertion definition, remove an assertion referenced by a gate, or loosen an assertion without a verified authorization Decision; observe a raw handled TypeError tagged unclassified_runtime_error."
resolution: Classified assurance declaration and reference TypeError refusals at the shared action boundary as canonical invalid_argument_value usage errors while preserving unexpected non-TypeError failures.
expected_result: "Malformed definitions, referenced removals, and unauthorized weakening return host-consistent typed usage refusals without entering unexpected-error capture; registry, evaluator, and storage faults remain fail-closed."
actual_result: "All three live fault classes now return PmCliError exit 2 through the shared CLI/SDK/MCP path; nested assurance fields are checked before string operations, and a deliberately corrupt registry still returns the original generic assurance_registry_invalid failure."
component: SDK assurance action transport
customer_impact: Fresh high issues block the fail-closed reliability gate and would block the next publication until fixed or aged out.
